WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.260
Lights out.

2
00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:05.060
Your body goes still, but
your brain keeps working.

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.270
All night, your brain
waves slow right down,

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.290
then speed up again, over and over.

5
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.380
And in one stage, a dream bubble appears.

6
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.290
That stage is called REM.

7
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.870
So if most dreaming happens in
REM, what are the other stages for?

8
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.650
In this mission, you'll follow your brain
down from light stage 1 to deep stage

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.600
4.

10
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.430
You'll see why REM is so
strange: darting eyes,

11
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.830
a busy brain, paralysed arms and legs.

12
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.040
And you'll track the
cycle: about 90 minutes,

13
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.580
repeating 4 to 5 times a night.

14
00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:45.560
Your mission: find out what the
other stages of sleep are for.
